    "one_liner": "Python leads at 21.25% but posts the largest year-over-year decline among the top 5, while C surges to second and Go drops from 7th to 16th.",
    "goal": "Give technology decision-makers a clear, data-backed view of which programming languages are rising, falling, and holding steady so they can align hiring, training, and tooling investments with industry momentum."
